:: Robin Hole Talk [nobr]
<<effects>>

<!--

-->

<<if $phase is 0>>
  "I heard some other orphans talking about something like there being a hole here somewhere and if you stick your butt through it in the evening a monster on the other side will do something amazing that makes you feel very relaxed and good." <<he>> says.
  <!--  -->
  <br><br>

  "What do you think about it? Do you think it's true?"
  <br><br>

  <br>
  <<link [[Yes|$passage]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
  <br>
  <<link [[No|$passage]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>><<llove>><<ldom>>
  <br>
  <<if $awareness gte 300>>
  <<link [[It's just a large gloryhole|$passage]]>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>><<llove>>
  <</if>>
<<elseif $phase is 1>>
  "It does sound wonderful doesn't it? A kind monster helping people relax "
  <br><br>
  <<if $NPCName.dom lte 5>>
  "Do you think we should go look for it later? Or wait, maybe I should look for it by myself since you probably have better things to do."
  <<else>>
  "How about we look for it later? If you aren't interested I could look for it by myself."
  <</if>>
  
  <<link [[Let's search together|Robin hole]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
  <<link [[I'll leave it to you|Robin hole]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
  <<link [[Leave it to me|Robin hole]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<<elseif $phase is 2>>
  "Oh... That's too bad, a kind monster helping people relax sounded nice but I guess that was too much to hope for."
  <<endevent "RHoleT" 0>>
<<elseif $phase is 3>>
  "Oh... Uh, what's a gloryhole?"
  <<link [[Explain frankly|Robin hole explain]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
  <<link [[Explain delicately|Robin hole explain]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
  <<link [[Be evasive|Robin hole explain]]>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Robin Hole Explain [nobr]
<<effects>>



:: Robin Hole Solo Find Old[nobr]
<<set $location to "unusedroom">><<effects>>
<!--What exactly was I thinking of when writing this? Was the idea that you'd prepare things so that you could lead Robin to the hole and have it work as he expects it to? Seems like it, -->

You find what seems like the hole Robin was talking about.

As expected there is nothing special about it, it's just a hole between an old supply closet and a bedroom that seems to be used to store broken furniture, you do notice some cigarette butts and cleaned areas in the room and assume some orphans are using it as an hangout.

<<link [[Seal off the room|$passage]]>><</link>>

You rearrange the furniture to make it nearly impossible to get in through the door unless you know exactly what you're doing.


<<if $container.lastLocation is "home">>
  <<link [[Bring containers here|$passage]]>>
    <<set $container.lastLocation to $location>>
  <</link>>


  
:: Robin Hole Solo Find 1 [nobr]
<<effects>>

Eventually you find an empty supply closet on the bottom floor of the orphanage, back of it is a concrete wall that has a smooth hole through it into darkness at a waist level. This must be the hole Robin talked about, it does seem suitable for pushing your butt through.

<<link [[Try it out|Robin Hole Solo Find Try]]>><</link>>
<<if "get stuck" is 1>> <!--Should check that if this coerces into true or not... Or I could just add an actual condition-->
  <<link [[Crawl through the hole|Robin Hole Solo Find Stuck]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
  <<link [[Crawl through the hole|Robin Hole Solo Find 2]]>>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
<</if>>
<<link [[Search for the other side from outside|Robin Hole Solo Find 2]]>>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<<link [[Memorize the location and leave|$passage]]>><</link>>

