:: Robin Hole Solo Find 2 [nobr]
<<effects>>
<!-- Shouldn't make the room too complicated to describe, or actually just describing whatever you see without making you assume too much about it's purpose seems fine even if it's some weird half basement technically outside the orphanage but attached to it-->
<<if $phase is 0>>
  You crawl through the hole, and get into a dark basement. The only light comes from the supply closet door you left open. You squint your eyes and explore the room. Piles of broken and old furniture fill the room. You find a metal door on one wall, easily opening it up you find yourself outside, at the side of the orphanage and at the bottom of a few steps that bury the door of the room halfway below ground.
  <br>
  <br>
  With the light from outside you notice that
  <!-- Would there be  any point to not just automatically finding the door? Chance to change your mind? Just to reinforce that it's pitch black if all doors are closed? 
  <<link [[Keep exploring|$passage]]>><</link>>
  <<link [[Go back|$passage]]>><</link>>
  -->
<<elseif $phase is 1>>
  You can't find a path to the other side of the hole anywhere near the closet. After some thinking you conclude the concrete wall is part of orphanages outer walls and so you search outside and on the side of the orphanage you indeed find a door few steps below ground level in an extension that must be where the hole leads. Trying the door it opens up easily and you see that other than the hole the room is littered with broken and old furniture.
  <br>
  <br>
  After a more careful search you notice that
<</if>>
there's some new looking trash littered around and dust free spots one could sit at comfortably. Seems like the room sees occasional use, other orphans perhaps?
<<if "$code, lock or block" == "block">>
Looking at the door you notice you could easily block it from being opened at all.
<<elseif "$code, lock or block" == "code">>
Looking at the door you notice a code lock that hasn't been set on it.
<!--Insert another weird/ridiculous excuse that allows you to set the door to be openable by only you without introducing the idea of just buying and using locks however you want-->
<<elseif "$code, lock or block" == "lock">>
Looking at the door you notice that it has a broken lock you could easily replace with your own.
<</if>>
<!--
Locking out whoever's been using the room and use it for yourself in some way.
-->

Seems like there's no monster or anything that special about the hole. Robin might be disappointed to hear that,
<!-- Is this an ok way to suggest this? -->
perhaps you could do something to make <<him>> believe it's real.

<<link [[Seal off the room|$passage]]>><</link>>
<<link [[Wait|$passage]]>><</link>>
<<link [[Leave|$passage]]>><</link>>

